<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belmanna riots</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belmanna riots were an uprising of labourers at Roxborough in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> in May 1876, named after Corporal Belmanna, a police officer who had shot a woman during unrest on an estate. The crowd killed Belmanna and burned buildings before troops restored order. Shaken by the riots, the island's assembly gave up its powers, and Tobago became a crown colony in 1877.</p></div>
